# StatBand - a row of big numbers split by hairlines (two per row on a phone). Each Stat holds its value in the slot
# (a Span, or a CountUp that counts up when it comes into view) and its label under it.
#   StatBand { Stat(label: "appointments a month") { CountUp(to: "12,400") }  Stat(label: "shops") { Span "850" } }
# look: "tiles" puts each number on its own soft tile, left-aligned, for a card inside an app (what the bot did this
# month: “0 bookings it closed by itself”); the default is the landing's band, centred between hairlines.
#   StatBand(look: "tiles") { Stat(label: "bookings it closed by itself") { Span "12" }  Stat(label: "orders it took by itself") { Span "5" } }
# While the numbers load, put a Skeleton in each Stat's slot.
# shadcn-for-muten · parts · no deps · kit.css (.cx-statband).
part StatBand(look: text = "") { Stack class("cx-statband") data(look: $look) { slot } }
part Stat(label: text) { Stack class("cx-statband-cell") { Stack class("cx-statband-value") { slot }  Span "{$label}" class("cx-statband-label") } }
